---
title: Matcha Shortbread Cookies Recipe
image: https://www.biggerbolderbaking.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/Matcha-Shortbread-Thumbnail-scaled.jpg
prep time: 15 minutes
tags: Matcha Cookies, Matcha Shortbread, Matcha Shortbread Cookies
servings: 36
course: Dessert
source: https://www.biggerbolderbaking.com/matcha-shortbread-cookies-recipe/#wprm-recipe-container-42258
cuisine: Scottish
cook time: 22 minutes
---

Beat @butter{1%cup}(softened), @sugar{1/2%cup}, and @vanilla extract{1%teaspoon} together with an electric mixer for a few minutes until light and fluffy.

In a separate bowl, combine @all-purpose flour{2.25%cups}, @matcha powder{4%tablespoons}, and @salt{1/4%teaspoon}, and gradually add this mixture to the butter mixture.

> If your dough is too crumbly, add small amounts of butter (softened) until it sticks together.

Gather and press the dough into a flattened disk and chill until firm, about ~{120%minutes}.

When ready to bake, preheat the oven to 325°F (165°C) and line 2 #baking sheets{} with parchment paper.

Roll out dough to a 1/4 inch (6mm) thickness on a floured surface and cut circles with a #2-inch (5cm) round cutter{}. Place cookies on the prepared baking sheet. Gather and reroll any scraps.

Sprinkle cookies with @sugar{}(as needed), tapping gently so that the sugar sticks, and then bake for ~{18-22%minutes}, until the cookies are dry and firm (they should not take on any color). Transfer to a wire rack to let cool completely.

Store in an airtight container at room temperature for up to 3 days.